Link xdvipsk against the system libtiff instead of its bundled libtiff
4.7.0 in texk/xdvipsk/thirdparty/libtiff.

- configure.ac: find libtiff-4 with pkg-config.
- Makefile.am: drop the bundled libtiff.a and use LIBTIFF_CFLAGS/_LIBS.
- loadTIFF.cpp: include the public tiffio.h instead of the private
  tiffiop.h, and drop the FreeImage-style platform layer that replaced
  libtiff's tif_unix.c (TIFFOpen, _TIFFmalloc and friends, and the
  _TIFFerrorHandler/_TIFFwarningHandler globals); the system libtiff
  provides those. The stream opener becomes a static bitmapTIFFOpen(),
  since libtiff's own TIFFFdOpen() takes a file descriptor, and it
  installs the same silent handlers through TIFFSetWarningHandler()
  and TIFFSetErrorHandler().

Gentoo-specific; applies after the system-libjpeg patch.

